items.q:
1. What is the output?
int a = 5, b = 2;
System.out.println(a / b);
System.out.println(a % b);
System.out.println((double) a / b);

2. What is the output and why?
String s1 = new String("hello");
String s2 = new String("hello");
String s3 = "hello";
String s4 = "hello";
System.out.println(s1 == s2);
System.out.println(s3 == s4);
System.out.println(s1.equals(s2));

3. What is the output?
int x = 5;
System.out.println(x++);
System.out.println(x);
System.out.println(++x);
System.out.println(x);

4. What is the output?
System.out.println(1 + 2 + "3");
System.out.println("1" + 2 + 3);
System.out.println("1" + (2 + 3));
System.out.println(1 + 2 + 3 + "!");

5. What is the output?
int count = 0;
boolean a = (count++ > 0) || (++count > 0);
System.out.println(count);

int count2 = 0;
boolean b = (count2++ > 0) && (++count2 > 0);
System.out.println(count2);

6. Rewrite using the ternary operator:
String result;
if (marks >= 60) {
    result = "Pass";
} else {
    result = "Fail";
}
And: is it always better to use ternary here?

7. What is the output? Explain the bitwise operations.
int a = 0b1010;  // 10
int b = 0b1100;  // 12
System.out.println(a & b);
System.out.println(a | b);
System.out.println(a ^ b);
System.out.println(~a);

8. Will this code compile? If so, what is the output?
byte b = 10;
b = b + 5;
b += 5;
System.out.println(b);
